The attached image, Figure 7D, is a Western blot demonstrating the forms of IL-1β in the supernatant and cell lysate of bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). It confirms that Nano-11 induces the active, secreted 17 kD form of IL-1β, especially when BMDCs are primed with LPS. The cell lysate shows the presence of pro-IL-1β (30 kD) when cells are primed with LPS, which is then cleaved to the active 17 kD form and secreted, as evidenced by the strong 17 kD band in the supernatant for LPS + Nano-11 treatment. This supports the finding that Nano-11 promotes IL-1β maturation and secretion, a key pro-inflammatory cytokine.